❓Question
Given a string s containing lowercase and uppercase letters, return the length of the longest palindrome that can be built using those letters.
Letters are case-sensitive, so "Aa" is not considered a palindrome.

Example 1
Input:  s = "abccccdd"
Output: 7
One possible palindrome is: dccaccd

✅Approach
Use a HashMap to count the frequency of every character.
For every frequency:
If it is even, we can use the entire count.
If it is odd, we can use value - 1, leaving one character unused.
If there is at least one odd-frequency character, we can place one of those characters in the middle.
Return the resulting length.

For example:
a = 1
b = 1
c = 4
d = 2

We can use:
c → 4
d → 2
a → 0 (from its pair)
b → 0 (from its pair)
Then use one odd character in the middle:
4 + 2 + 1 = 7

Code
class Solution {
    public int longestPalindrome(String s) {
        HashMap<Character, Integer> map = new HashMap<>();
        for(int i = 0; i < s.length(); i++){
            char ch = s.charAt(i);
            map.put(ch, map.getOrDefault(ch, 0) + 1);
        }
        boolean isOdd = false;
        int longestString = 0;
        for(int value : map.values()){
            if(value % 2 == 0){
                longestString += value;
            }else{
                longestString += value - 1;
                isOdd = true;
            }
        }
        if(isOdd){
            longestString += 1;
        }
        return longestString;
    }
}

Time Complexity
O(n)
Space Complexity
O(n)
